            "claim": "Memory/resource leak: session started on worker thread is never cleaned up if bridge is destroyed before queued completion runs. The lambda captures session but if bridge dies, the lambda is dropped without destroying the session.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "const QString err = connectCoreOnly(uri, &session);\n\n        QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [this, uri, err, session]() {"
        },
        {
            "claim": "The code change removes m_pendingSession but the destructor no longer has any mechanism to clean up a session that was started on the worker thread but never completed. The old code used m_pendingSession.exchange(nullptr) in the destructor to clean it up.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "// A connect whose queued completion never ran (it was dropped with\n    // `this`) left its session pending. It was never started, so no\n    // worker is calling onFrame; destroy it like any other.\n    if (qttune_session_t* pending = m_pendingSession.exchange(nullptr)) {\n        qttune_session_destroy(pending);\n    }"
        },
        {
            "claim": "The updateValues change breaks the documented contract: the comment says 'Values and history update regardless' but the code now only updates values for subscribed entries.",
            "file": "app/qttunebridge.cpp",
            "quote": "if (e.id == pair.first && e.subscribed) {"
        }
    ],
    "questions": [
        "Where is applyConnectedState(session, uri) called in the new connectSessionAsync? The diff shows removal of old code but doesn't show the replacement that should use the session.",
        "Is qttune_session_start async or does it block? If frames can arrive immediately after start, is there a race between frame arrival and GUI thread taking ownership?",
        "What is the complete new lambda body in connectSessionAsync? The diff appears truncated."
